
== pc1
C:\>dnsd start
DNS server listening on UDP port 53.
C:\>dnsd add web.example.com 10.0.0.2
C:\>dnsd list
DNS server is running. 1 name, 0 queries answered.
10.0.0.2 web.example.com

== r2
r2>enable
r2#configure terminal
r2(config)#interface g0/0
r2(config-if)#ip address 10.0.0.2 255.255.255.0
r2(config-if)#no shutdown
r2(config-if)#exit
r2(config)#ip host files.example.com 10.0.0.1
r2(config)#ip dns server
r2(config)#end

== r1
r1>enable
r1#configure terminal
r1(config)#interface g0/0
r1(config-if)#ip address 10.0.0.1 255.255.255.0
r1(config-if)#no shutdown
r1(config-if)#exit
r1(config)#ip name-server 10.0.0.10
r1(config)#ip domain-name example.com
r1(config)#ip host printer 10.0.0.1
r1(config)#end
r1#ping web
Translating "web"...domain server (10.0.0.10) [OK]
Type escape sequence to abort.
Sending 5, 100-byte ICMP Echos to 10.0.0.2, timeout is 2 seconds:
!!!!!
Success rate is 100 percent (5/5), round-trip min/avg/max = 27/31/50 usec
r1#ping nosuch
Translating "nosuch"...domain server (10.0.0.10)
% Unrecognized host or address, or protocol not running.
r1#ping printer
Type escape sequence to abort.
Sending 5, 100-byte ICMP Echos to 10.0.0.1, timeout is 2 seconds:
!!!!!
Success rate is 100 percent (5/5), round-trip min/avg/max = 0/0/0 usec
r1#show hosts
Default domain is example.com
Name/address lookup uses domain service
Name servers are 10.0.0.10

Codes: UN - unknown, EX - expired, OK - OK, ?? - revalidate
       temp - temporary, perm - permanent
       NA - Not Applicable None - Not defined

Host                      Port Flags      Age Type   Address(es)
printer                   None (perm, OK)  0   IP      10.0.0.1

